      "body": "## Summary\n\nThe backend probe in `python/sglang/srt/utils/video_decoder.py` only catches `ImportError` and `RuntimeError` when importing `torchcodec`. A torchcodec wheel that installs cleanly but whose native library fails to load (e.g. an FFmpeg version mismatch) raises `OSError` instead, which escapes the guard and breaks the whole `sglang.srt.utils.common` import chain — on hosts where decord is installed and would work fine.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `OSError` to the fallback `except` tuple so the decord fallback also engages for unloadable torchcodec native libraries.\n\n## Testing\n\n- [x] Reproduced on a deployment host with a broken torchcodec native lib: `sglang.launch_server` failed at import time before the change; after it, the decord fallback engaged and the server started normally.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40809037298](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40809037298)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40809037225](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40809037225)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40809037116](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40809037116)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
